# build_tables.py writes its report beside the records it reads. On 2026-09-23 an audit agent ran
# it, the files landed in a PUBLISHED records directory, and a git add -A swept them into the v1.2.1
# tag and from there into the Zenodo deposit. One of them stated the cell cost from the FIRST record
# alone, which for gcp-easy was the un-repriced $29.28, so the deposit carried a surface refuting the
# paper frontier column it was cut to support.
results/*/*/records/tables.json
results/*/*/records/tables.txt
